DOM(Document Object Model):a representation of an HTML document created by the browser which allows JS to interact with the page
* Browser receives the HTML file
* Browser reads the HTMl line by line
* Browser converts HTML into objects 
* Browser organizes the objects into a structure 
* That structure becomes DOM

.document
  .HTMl
    .body
	  .h1
	  .p
Every part of the DOM is a node

1. Parent:An element that contains another element 
2. Child:An element inside another element 
3. Sibling:Elements at the same level

